C31 patch B -- Ctrl+K opens the OVERLAY, not only the shell (5 lines, one file).
Generated with git diff against main@35bb3be and verified with "git apply --check".
Apply:  git apply tools/patches/c31-palette-overlay.patch
C8 already resolves Ctrl+K to Command::OpenPalette and GalleryWindow routes it to OpenPalette(),
so the patch only attaches the overlay to that shell and opens both from the same call. Painting
the commands is the renderer job (GalleryRenderer.hpp is C29): the list is overlay_.Build(w, h).
The overlay takes precedence on keys, so the shell highlight is no longer what is painted --
RunPalette() still uses palette_.Highlighted() for the entry.
